<!--meta {"lead": "A form field keeps a control's label, help, error and counter together, in the same order and spacing, so every question on every HairPop form reads the same way.", "description": "The wrapper every input uses: label, optional marker, help, error and counter, with the wiring for each.", "pills": ["Layout primitive", "Status: stable"], "variants": "label + control, + help, + error, + counter, + addons, optional marker, group (fieldset), choice (single checkbox)", "states": "default, focus, invalid, disabled, read-only", "sources": ["pages/account-settings/invalid", "pages/sign-in/invalid", "pages/booking-request/invalid", "pages/care-and-review/invalid", "dialogs/filter-braiders/invalid", "dialogs/cookie-preferences/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Every <a href="text-field.html">text field</a>, <a href="textarea.html">textarea</a> and <a href="select.html">select</a> sits in a <code>.field</code>. It is not a control; it is the layout and wiring around one: the label above, help and error below, joined to the control by <code>for</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code>. Groups of <a href="checkbox.html">checkboxes</a> or <a href="radio-group.html">radios</a> use a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code> instead.</p>
  <p>The wrapper is a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>, never a <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>: putting help or errors inside the label makes them part of the control's accessible name.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <div class="field" style="width: min(100%, 22rem);"><label class="field__label" for="ff-anat">Phone <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label><input class="input" id="ff-anat" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" value="416-555-01" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="ff-anat-error ff-anat-help"><span class="field__help" id="ff-anat-help">Nia may text you about timing.</span><span class="field__error" id="ff-anat-error">Enter a 10-digit phone number like 416-555-0148.</span></div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 12%; top: 10%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 40%; top: 10%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 80%; top: 36%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 70%; top: 60%;" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 86%; top: 82%;" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Label</b><small><code>.field__label</code>, label font, <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code>.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Optional marker</b><small><code>.optional</code>, regular weight, muted.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Control</b><small>Input, textarea or select.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Help</b><small><code>.field__help</code>, body-sm, muted; stays visible while an error shows.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Error</b><small><code>.field__error</code>, body-sm, danger text with a warning glyph that is hidden from screen readers; below the help, first in <code>aria-describedby</code>.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <p>Parts are stacked with <code>--space-1</code> (4px) between them in this order: label, control, help, error, counter. Fields in a form are <code>--space-4</code> (16px) apart, set by the form, not the field.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]Label only; with help; with counter; with a unit addon; group in a <code>fieldset.field</code>; choice mode, where a single checkbox carries its own label.}}
<div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ff-v1">Name</label><input class="input" id="ff-v1" type="text" autocomplete="name" value="Maya Chen"></div>
<div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ff-v2">New password</label><input class="input" id="ff-v2" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" aria-describedby="ff-v2-help"><span class="field__help" id="ff-v2-help">Use at least 12 characters.</span></div>
<div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ff-v3">Your review</label><textarea class="textarea textarea--auto-grow" id="ff-v3" aria-describedby="ff-v3-count">Nia explained each step and the braids feel comfortable.</textarea><span class="field__counter" id="ff-v3-count">56 of 500 characters</span></div>
<div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ff-v4">Maximum price</label><div class="input-group"><span class="addon" aria-hidden="true">$</span><input class="input" id="ff-v4" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="10" value="150"></div></div>
<fieldset class="field"><legend>Braid size</legend><div class="choice-group choice-group--inline"><label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="ff-size"><span>Small</span></label><label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="ff-size" checked><span>Medium</span></label><label class="choice"><input type="radio" name="ff-size"><span>Large</span></label></div></fieldset>
<div class="field"><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" id="ff-v5" checked><span>Remember my optional usage choices</span></label></div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="The wrapper has no size; it takes the size of its control and the form column."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>The field shows its control's state and adds the error. The label never changes colour, so state is carried by the control edge plus the error text (SC 1.4.1).</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Invalid</th><th scope="col">Read-only</th><th scope="col">Disabled</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Email</th>
        <td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffs-1">Email</label><input class="input" id="ffs-1" type="email" value="maya.chen@example.com"></div></td>
        <td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffs-2">Email</label><input class="input" id="ffs-2" type="email" value="maya.chen@example.com" data-state="focus"></div></td>
        <td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffs-3">Email</label><input class="input" id="ffs-3" type="email" value="maya.chen@" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="ffs-3-e"><span class="field__error" id="ffs-3-e">Enter an email address like name@example.com.</span></div></td>
        <td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffs-4">Email</label><input class="input" id="ffs-4" type="email" value="maya.chen@example.com" readonly></div></td>
        <td><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffs-5">Email</label><input class="input" id="ffs-5" type="email" value="maya.chen@example.com" disabled></div></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<div class="field"><span class="field__label" aria-hidden="true">Phone <span class="optional">(optional)</span></span><input class="input" type="tel" value="416-555-01" aria-invalid="true" aria-label="Phone (optional), preview"><span class="field__help">Nia may text you about timing.</span><span class="field__error">Enter a 10-digit phone number.</span></div>{{/themes}}
  <p>Theme previews repeat the markup, so they omit ids; production fields always link help and error with <code>aria-describedby</code>.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Labels always sit above the control; never beside it, at any width. Side labels break at 200% zoom and in translation.</li>
    <li>The field fills its column; long labels, help, errors and counters wrap, and a word longer than the line ("name@example.com" at 200% text) breaks instead of overflowing (<code>overflow-wrap: anywhere</code>).</li>
    <li>An input group keeps the control and its addon on one line at 320px; the control shrinks and the addon keeps its width.</li>
    <li>Two fields share a row only from 768px and only when they are short and related (see <a href="form-layout.html">form layout</a>).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The field reads only text tokens: <code>--color-fg-default</code> for the label, <code>--color-fg-muted</code> for help and the optional marker, <code>--color-danger-fg</code> for errors and <code>--color-fg-subtle</code> for the counter. Each passes 4.5:1 on canvas, surface and raised surfaces in both themes.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>No role of its own. <code>&lt;label for="id"&gt;</code> names the control (SC 1.3.1, 3.3.2); <code>aria-describedby</code> lists the error first, then help, then any announced addon ("km"), then the counter, so the most urgent information is read first; <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> on the control exactly while the error shows. Groups use <code>&lt;fieldset class="field"&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code>; the fieldset carries the description and every option carries <code>aria-invalid</code>.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Reaches the control only; labels, help and errors are not focusable.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The control shows focus. When a submit fails, focus goes to the error summary, whose links move focus to each field.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>Errors appear once the person has changed a field and left it, or on submit, not while typing; once shown, they re-validate on input and disappear as soon as the value is fixed. The error's warning glyph uses CSS alternative text <code>""</code> so it is not announced. Counters say "56 of 500 characters", never "56 / 500", and are announced politely only after a pause near the limit.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Label on card|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Help on card|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Error on card|--color-danger-fg|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Error on page|--color-danger-fg|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Help in dialog|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface-raised|4.5}}
    {{pair:Error in dialog|--color-danger-fg|--color-bg-surface-raised|4.5}}
    {{pair:Counter on card|--color-fg-subtle|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>Errors appear without animation so their position is stable for magnifier users.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>The label is part of the tap target for its control.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Label: a noun in sentence case ("Phone"), no colon.</li>
    <li>Optional marker: "(optional)" after the label, only when most fields are required.</li>
    <li>Help: why or how, one sentence ("Nia may text you about timing.").</li>
    <li>Error: what to do, with an example ("Enter a 10-digit phone number like 416-555-0148.").</li>
    <li>Counter: "56 of 500 characters"; over the limit the error states it: "Shorten this to 200 characters or fewer."</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffd-1">Email</label><input class="input" id="ffd-1" type="email" value="maya.chen@" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="ffd-1-e"><span class="field__error" id="ffd-1-e">Enter an email address like name@example.com.</span></div></div><figcaption>A <code>&lt;div class="field"&gt;</code> with the error linked by id.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><label class="field" for="ffd-2"><span class="field__label">Email</span><input class="input" id="ffd-2" type="email" value="maya.chen@" aria-invalid="true"><span class="field__error">Enter a valid email address.</span></label></div><figcaption>The mocks use <code>&lt;label class="field"&gt;</code> around the error, so the error is read as part of the label.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffd-3">Maximum price</label><input class="input" id="ffd-3" type="number" value="150" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="ffd-3-e"><span class="field__error" id="ffd-3-e">Enter a price of at least $160 for this style.</span></div></div><figcaption>The error states the fix with a real number.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="ffd-4">Preferred time</label><input class="input" id="ffd-4" type="text" value="Sun 25 Oct, 11:00 am" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="ffd-4-e"><span class="field__error" id="ffd-4-e">Enter a valid value to continue.</span></div></div><figcaption>The mocks' fallback error "Enter a valid value to continue." says nothing about what is wrong.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Label|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Help / optional marker|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Error|--color-danger-fg}}
      {{tok:Counter|--color-fg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Label font|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Help and error font|--text-body-sm}}
      {{tok:Counter font|--text-caption}}
      {{tok:Gap between parts|--space-1}}
      {{tok:Gap between fields|--space-4}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;div class="field"&gt;
  &lt;label class="field__label" for="phone"&gt;Phone &lt;span class="optional"&gt;(optional)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input class="input" id="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel"
         aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="phone-error phone-help"&gt;
  &lt;span class="field__help" id="phone-help"&gt;Nia may text you about timing.&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="field__error" id="phone-error"&gt;Enter a 10-digit phone number like 416-555-0148.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.field</code></td><td>Vertical stack, 4px gaps, <code>min-width: 0</code>; on a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>, or on a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> for a group.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.field__label</code> + <code>.optional</code></td><td>Label row with an optional marker.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.field__help</code></td><td>Muted help text.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.field__error</code></td><td>Danger text with a warning glyph hidden from assistive technology.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.field__counter</code>, <code>[data-over="true"]</code></td><td>Right-aligned count; danger colour when over the limit.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.input-group</code> + <code>.addon</code></td><td>Prefix or suffix (currency, unit) or an attached "Show" button; an addon without <code>aria-hidden</code> joins the description.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/account-settings/invalid|email error}}
    {{mock:pages/sign-in/invalid|email error under the summary}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/invalid|preferred-time group error}}
    {{mock:pages/care-and-review/invalid|rating group and review errors}}
    {{mock:dialogs/filter-braiders/invalid|price error in a dialog}}
    {{mock:dialogs/cookie-preferences/default|choice field}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: every mock field was a <code>&lt;label class="field"&gt;</code> wrapping control and error (now a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code>); no field had help text; the default error copy "Enter a valid value to continue." gave no fix; the error's "⚠" glyph was announced by screen readers (now CSS alternative text <code>""</code>); descriptions listed help before the error (now the error is read first); a bare <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> put the error directly against the options (now <code>fieldset.field</code> keeps the 4px rhythm).</p>
</section>
